// The same unset read as `native_build_unset_global.oskl`, but the only
// assignment to `later` sits in a function the program never calls. The name is
// assigned *somewhere*, so the compiler accepts the program and the slot is
// unset at run time: the binary must fail with "undefined variable 'later'" and
// exit 70, exactly like the hosted engine.
//
// This is the case a per-proto analysis would miss: the assignment is in another
// proto, so the top-level read has to be judged against the whole program.
fn never() { later = 5; }
print(later);
